<title>UK: UK Nuclear Electric asks for Sizewell fuel reload.</title>
<headline>UK Nuclear Electric asks for Sizewell fuel reload.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Nuclear Electric (NE) has exercised an option in a fuel supply contract for a further reload of fuel for the Sizewell B power station in 1999, a statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;NE has issued a letter of intent to BNFL (British Nuclear Fuels plc) for a further reload of fuel for the Sizewell B power station,&quot; the statement from BNFL said. &quot;NE has exercised an option, within the existing contract for fuel, to be made in 1998 and delivered in 1999. This will extend the total contract scope to cover three reloads.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
